1	# flagship_dw — L-generalize the decoder TC backward dW-spec / LN-vec / Muon-2D enumeration
2	
3	AREA: `csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh` (+ pinned call sites in
4	`csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh`).
5	
6	GOAL: generalize every HARDCODED 2-layer enumeration in the decoder TC backward
7	path to a general `dec::kLayers` form, so the flagship TC megakernel
8	(d=1600, L=48; layout `decoder_flagship_layout.cuh`, `kDecNumTensors=582`)
9	FUNCTIONALLY processes all 48 layers. Every edit is BYTE-IDENTICAL at L=2
10	(`dec::kLayers==2`) so `tests/hw/test_decoder_tc.py` (d=128/L=2) is unaffected:
11	the new constant `kDecNumDwSpecs` equals 9 at L=2, the spec/bias/loop bounds
12	collapse to the current `9`/`8`, and the new index formulas reproduce the exact
13	current literal tables verbatim at L=2 (proven below).
14	
15	## Verification of the index formulas at L=2 (must reproduce the literals)
16	
17	Per-layer 12-tensor stride (codegen `_decoder_param_sizes`, megakernel_codegen.py
18	596-617): for layer `li`, tensor index `2+12*li+r` with r∈{0..11} =
19	{in_w,in_b, out_w,out_b, n1_w,n1_b,n2_w,n2_b, ff0_w,ff0_b, ff2_w,ff2_b}.
20	Tail: `2+12*L+{0,1,2,3}` = {norm_w, norm_b, out_w, out_b}.
21	
22	dW weights `tidx(li,kind) = 2 + 12*li + {0,2,8,10}[kind]`, bias `+1`; head
23	weight `2+12*L+2`, bias `+1`:
24	- L=2: s0..s7 → wi {2,4,10,12, 14,16,22,24}, bi {3,5,11,13, 15,17,23,25};
25	  head wi=2+24+2=28, bi=29. EXACTLY the current `wi[9]/bi[9]` + `spec[8]`.
26	
27	LN-vec slots: v∈[0,4L): `li=v/4, kind=v%4`, tidx `6+12*li+kind`;
28	v=4L → norm_w `2+12*L`; v=4L+1 → norm_b `2+12*L+1`.
29	- L=2: {6,7,8,9, 18,19,20,21, 26,27}. EXACTLY the current `kLnVecTensorIdx[10]`.
30	
31	Muon-2D: mi=0 tok{0}, mi=1 pos{1}, mi∈[2,2+4L): `li=(mi-2)/4, kind=(mi-2)%4` →
32	{in_w 2+12li, out_w 4+12li, ff0_w 10+12li, ff2_w 12+12li}; mi=2+4L → out_w `2+12L+2`.
33	- L=2: {0,1, 2,4,10,12, 14,16,22,24, 28}. EXACTLY the current `kDecMuon2D[11]`.
34	
35	`dec_is_muon_2d(t)`: t∈{0,1} OR t==2+12L+2 OR (t∈[2,2+12L) AND (t-2)%12∈{0,2,8,10}).
36	- L=2: returns true for {0,1,2,4,10,12,14,16,22,24,28}. Same membership set.
37	
38	`kDecNumDwSpecs = 4*dec::kLayers + 1` (= 9 at L=2, 193 at L=48).
39	`kNumLnVec = 4*dec::kLayers + 2` (= 10 at L=2, 194 at L=48).
40	`kDecNumMuon2D = 4*dec::kLayers + 3` (= 11 at L=2, 195 at L=48). [tok+pos+head + 4/layer]
41	
42	---
43	
44	# FILE 1 — csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh
45	
46	## Edit 1.1 — LN-vec count + the `kLnVecTensorIdx` constant table → formula
47	
48	The `__device__ __constant__ int kLnVecTensorIdx[...]` brace-list cannot be filled
49	by a runtime loop at L=48 (194 entries). Replace it with a `constexpr` index
50	formula `dec_lnvec_tensor_idx(v)` consumed by `dectc_lnvec_reduce`. `kNumLnVec`
51	and `kLnVecElems` become L-general (drive the HBM `lnvec` workspace carve, which
52	is already sized from `kLnVecElems` everywhere — no other change needed).
53	
54	OLD:
55	```
56	// ── LN vector-grad partials layout (the 10 tile-local γ/β grads). Order MUST
57	//    match dec_layout tensor indices {6,7,8,9,18,19,20,21,26,27}. We store them
58	//    densely [10 x kD] per CTA; the P2 reduce maps them back by tensor index. ──
59	constexpr int kNumLnVec = 10;                 // n1_w,n1_b,n2_w,n2_b ×L + norm_w,norm_b
60	constexpr int kLnVecElems = kNumLnVec * dec::kD;   // 10 * 128 = 1280
61	// The dec_layout tensor index of each LN-vector slot, in our dense order.
62	__device__ __constant__ int kLnVecTensorIdx[kNumLnVec] = {
63	    6, 7, 8, 9,        // L0 n1.w, n1.b, n2.w, n2.b
64	    18, 19, 20, 21,    // L1 n1.w, n1.b, n2.w, n2.b
65	    26, 27             // norm.w, norm.b
66	};
67	```
68	
69	NEW:
70	```
71	// ── LN vector-grad partials layout (the tile-local γ/β grads). Dense order:
72	//    4 slots/layer (n1.w,n1.b,n2.w,n2.b) for li∈[0,L), then norm.w,norm.b. At L=2
73	//    this is {6,7,8,9,18,19,20,21,26,27} (the original 10-slot table). We store
74	//    them densely [kNumLnVec x kD] per CTA; the P2 reduce maps them back by tensor
75	//    index via dec_lnvec_tensor_idx (a formula — a __constant__ array can't be
76	//    filled by a loop at L=48). L-GENERAL: kNumLnVec = 4*L+2. ──
77	constexpr int kNumLnVec = 4 * dec::kLayers + 2;   // n1_w,n1_b,n2_w,n2_b ×L + norm_w,norm_b
78	constexpr int kLnVecElems = kNumLnVec * dec::kD;  // (4*L+2)*kD  (1280 at L=2)
79	// dec_layout tensor index of LN-vector dense slot v. v∈[0,4L): li=v/4, kind=v%4 →
80	// 6+12*li+kind (n1.w/b,n2.w/b are tensor 6..9 of each 12-tensor layer block);
81	// v=4L → norm.w (2+12*L); v=4L+1 → norm.b (2+12*L+1). At L=2 reproduces the old
82	// kLnVecTensorIdx[10] EXACTLY ({6,7,8,9,18,19,20,21,26,27}).
83	__host__ __device__ __forceinline__ int dec_lnvec_tensor_idx(int v) {
84	    const int Lx4 = 4 * dec::kLayers;
85	    if (v < Lx4) return 6 + 12 * (v / 4) + (v % 4);
86	    return 2 + 12 * dec::kLayers + (v - Lx4);     // 2+12L (norm.w), 2+12L+1 (norm.b)
87	}
88	```
