686	# RISKS / NOTES
687	
688	1. **dW WORKSPACE (HBM) carves are L-general already** — `dec_dw_transpose_elems`
689	   (transpose scratch) and `dec_dw_part_floats`/`kDecDwMaxTiles` (split-K partials)
690	   loop `dec::kLayers`, and `dec_tc_acts_floats` loops `L`. The launcher's per-step
691	   dW work count is `n_dw = dectc_dw_total_tiles(spec)` (RUNTIME, counted from the
692	   spec array), NOT a 2-pinned literal — so it auto-scales to 193 specs at L=48.
693	   No L-pinned workspace literal remains.
694	
695	2. **DecTcSmem static-smem budget** — `spec[]` is the ONLY layer-dependent smem
696	   member (Edit 2.1). With SG_TUNED_DEC_DW_STAGE=1, sizeof(DecDwSpec)=72 B, so the
697	   array grows 9*72=648 B (L=2) → 193*72=13,896 B (L=48), a +13.25 KB delta.
698	   Budget at the flagship (d=1600, N=128): sA/sB/red depend on TILE_N + ring depth,
699	   NOT on d or L. At the DEFAULT flagship build (PIPE=1, STAGES=4 → SG_DEC_TC_DYNAMIC
700	   _SMEM=1) DecTcSmem lives in DYNAMIC smem (228 KB cap, certified at launch via
701	   cudaOccupancyMaxActiveBlocks) so the +13.25 KB is absorbed (est. total ~47 KB ≪
702	   228 KB → still 1 CTA/SM). At the static path (PIPE=0 or STAGES=2) the est. total
703	   at S=2 is ~31 KB < the 48 KB `static_assert` — so even a static flagship build
704	   passes the compile-time cap. At L=2 the member is byte-identical (spec[9]) → the
705	   17.64 KB measured default and the static_assert are unchanged. NOTE: I did NOT
706	   re-measure sizeof at L=48 (read-only; no build) — the lead's 2nd gate_command
707	   (compile_to_object on the flagship layout) is the real check; if the static path
708	   ever trips the 48 KB static_assert at L=48, the fix is to keep `spec` in smem but
709	   build it once (it already is) — or route to dynamic smem via the existing gate.
710	
711	3. **`#pragma unroll` over `kDecNumDwSpecs` in `dectc_dw_biases`** (Edit 1.11): at
712	   L=2 this fully unrolls a 9-trip prefix loop (byte-identical). At L=48 it fully
713	   unrolls a 193-trip loop and declares `pre[194]` (a per-thread local array,
714	   array-indexed → spills to local memory). This is FUNCTIONALLY correct and
715	   compiles, but at L=48 it is larger code + local-mem traffic in the bias pass.
716	   Left as `#pragma unroll` to GUARANTEE L=2 byte-identity (the gate). If L=48
717	   compile time / code size becomes an issue, change BOTH `#pragma unroll`s in this
718	   function to `#pragma unroll 1` — but ONLY behind `if constexpr (dec::kLayers>2)`
719	   or it perturbs the L=2 PTX. (Not needed for the functional flagship goal.)
